[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3325266982","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/2758#issuecomment-3325266982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2758","id":3325266982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7GM4wm","user":{"login":"mj12albert","id":4997971,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5OTc5NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4997971?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert","html_url":"https://github.com/mj12albert","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mj12albert/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-23T19:24:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-23T19:25:51Z","body":"@marcospgp Are you already using it? Or is it not working as you expected\n\nI guess the name `onClearErrors` is kind of misleading, it's called whenever one error is cleared e.g. when the user corrects a wrong value (and not errors plural as the name may imply), and the `errors` arg are the remaining errors in the form\n\nMaybe it would be helpful to provide the `name` of the field that was cleared of an error in the callback as well","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3325266982/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/comments/3329800415","html_url":"https://github.com/mui/base-ui/issues/2758#issuecomment-3329800415","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mui/base-ui/issues/2758","id":3329800415,"node_id":"IC_kwDOLW-eZs7GeLjf","user":{"login":"marcospgp","id":3464445,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0NjQ0NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3464445?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp","html_url":"https://github.com/marcospgp","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/marcospgp/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-24T16:35:42Z","updated_at":"2025-09-24T16:35:42Z","body":"@mj12albert personally I'm generally not finding form error handling useful, I just handle validation independently for each field because managing a dictionary of errors keyed by input field name seems like it would be way too much trouble.\n\nI just validate fields independently. And as long as they are validated when the form is submitted, then it works fine.\n\nThen if the server returns an error that the client-side validation did not catch, I just assume that that is a bug and display a generic error dialog, similarly to whenever any other unhandled exception would occur.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api